# The practice app and its question banks are left alone on purpose.
#
# A bank file is data, not code: a few hundred question objects, each written
# on as few lines as it takes to read one at a glance. Prettier reflows them to
# 80 columns, which turns a 171-question file into several thousand lines and
# makes the one thing anyone ever does here — scan the questions and add
# another — materially harder. The generators are the same shape.
#
# This is not "the old code we haven't got to yet". Everything Astro builds
# IS formatted; these files are the exception, and it's deliberate.
public/js/
src/data/lessons.js

# The app's own stylesheet, written one rule per line to stay scannable. Its
# companion, public/css/site.css, is new and IS formatted — the line is drawn
# between the original app and what was built around it, not between file types.
public/css/styles.css
